{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin with, you should choose your destination and calculate the distance."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly starts the process (init), justifies the redundant 'start' action, and directly describes the initial selection and calculation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "While doing so, continue to check if you need to book a train or a flight."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the action of evaluating which transport mode to book."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the answer is \"no\", then proceed to book a train. However, if the answer is \"yes\", then book a flight."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional phrasing implies the XOR decision point, routing the flow to either the train or flight booking action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "action:n7",
        "action:n10",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a code is available within 24 hours, the process will end."
      ],
      "justification": "This single condition applies symmetrically to both parallel transport paths, generating two identical check/decision/end sequences in the model."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, if 24 hours have passed, you should call a travel agency."
      ],
      "justification": "Covers the fallback action triggered when the 24-hour threshold is exceeded on either path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In that case, the process will end as well."
      ],
      "justification": "The closing statement confirms termination of the remaining execution paths, supporting the explicit termination actions and structural end nodes."
    }
  ],
  "mutations": [],
  "omissions": [
    {
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if a code is not available, you should cancel your journey."
      ],
      "reason": "The model lacks any branch or action to handle cancelling the journey when the code is unavailable."
    }
